  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Looks Like Rain** (2 reviews): Listener singles out Looks Like Rain as a standout moment of the night [5][6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Tangled Up In Blue**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [9]\n- **News Broadcast Dead Forever**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [9]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2025-04-26** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 161 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Recording is incomplete: it cuts out partly from technical problems, and the second set is missing because the transfer failed [1]\n- **deadco2025-04-26.Sir_Chu**: source not stated; 19 songs; 161 min [2]\n- **deadco2025-04-26.stelladew**: source not stated; 18 songs; 171 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [3]. Said about its sound: Listener calls this the best-sounding recording of this night they have heard [7]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Crowd 1st Set, Crowd 2nd Set [1]\n- Listener notes Dylan songs frame the night, bookending the rest of the show [7]\n- Lineup listed: Bobby Weir, Mickey Hart, John Mayer and Oteil Burbridge, under the title Dead Forever II [1]\n- Lineup listed: Bobby Weir, Mickey Hart, John Mayer and Oteil Burbridge, under the title Dead Forever II [2]\n- Lineup listed: Bobby Weir, Mickey Hart, John Mayer and Oteil Burbridge, at Sphere [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2025-04-26**: taped by r/GuestFlat6453; transferred by Hunter S II; source: Channels 1 & 2: Rode Wireless Micro > Rode Capture App > Phone [1]. Also: Recorded with Rode Wireless Micro on channels 1 and 2 into Rode Capture on a phone, then WAV, Reaper, 24-bit FLAC [1]\n- **deadco2025-04-26.Sir_Chu**: taped by Sir Chu Sonoran Dawg; transferred by Hunter S II; source: Zoom Iq7 > iPhone [2]. Also: Lineage is iPhone to WAV to Reaper to 24-bit FLAC [2]\n- **deadco2025-04-26.stelladew**: taped by Stella Dew; transferred by Stella Dew; source: Zoom iQ7 > iPhone [3]. Also: Transfer path was iPhone to WAV to Audacity to FLAC [3]",
